; maps.ini SAMPLE for klpm.c (re\pm_options.md B1; the format is a GUESS of klpm.c's kpm_maps_load, nothing else reads it).
; Copy to <Dog Days>\KLExpansion\Maps\maps.ini (or point [Match] Maps= at it). klhook\mkoverlay.py reads the same file for the names on the
; 'Map vote' row, so the order here IS the order of the menu entries: change this file, regenerate the overlay (KL_MATCH_MAPS=<file>).
; Id    = the folder name under KLExpansion\Maps (expansion maps) or the stock DD0n folder (KLHook.ini [Redirect]) - GUESS: nothing resolves it yet
; Name  = the menu text (47 characters at most)
; Slot  = the stock Fragile Alliance slot the map loads through (re\expansion.md; the stock maps are those slots themselves)
; Dog Days' own names are not in the exe's text I have read: "Dog Days Fnn" stands for the stock map of that slot (F01 is the Subway).
; Bundles (the playlist, [Match] Play=1/2): GUESS, kpm_parse_list reads Maps= by Id; no menu row picks a bundle yet.

